  "abilities": [],
  "behavior": "It patrols large areas from the air and seems able to detect threats from quite far away. Once it begins chasing a target, it may follow for a considerable distance and can be difficult to shake off.",
  "interactionWithPlayer": "It is extremely annoying and persistent. If Tiger Mosquitoes were already troublesome in Grounded, they can feel even worse in Grounded 2: they often spot you from far away and keep chasing for a long time.",
  "interactionWithCreatures": "They tend to show up at the worst possible moments, especially when the player is already fighting another creature or trying to escape. Their ability to keep circling above a fight can quickly turn a controlled situation into a much more complicated one.",
  "strategy": "Use Slashing weapons with a Fresh infusion and pay close attention to its strongest attacks. A perfect block (parry) has a good chance to knock the mosquito down, leaving it vulnerable for a few seconds; use that opening to deal as much damage as possible. If one appears while you are fighting another enemy, it is often worth making it a priority before it starts constantly interrupting the fight.",
